       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day (about 800 mg per dose). OTC use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inflammatory conditions or acute pain.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual range for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you really want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
